  "decision": {
    "answer": "SUPPORTS",
    "explanation": "The provided evidence from pmid-28787259 describes a phase I/II study involving 26 patients with relapsed/refractory ALK-positive Anaplastic Large Cell Lymphoma (ALCL) treated with crizotinib. The study reports an objective response rate of 90%, with complete response rates of 83% and 80% for different dose groups. This directly supports the claim that crizotinib is effective (sensitivity/response) in ALK fusion-positive ALCL. The evidence explicitly links the drug (crizotinib), the disease (ALCL), the molecular profile (ALK-positive, which implies ALK fusion), and the positive outcome (response rate).",
    "citations": [
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-28787259",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 551,
        "quote": "In this phase I/II study, 26 patients with relapsed/refractory ALK-positive ALCL were administered crizotinib orally twice daily in 28-day cycles as a single agent for an indefinite duration. Patients with relapsed ALCL achieved an objective response rate of 90%. The overall response rates for patients with ALCL treated at doses of 165 and 280 mg/m2 were 83% and 90%, respectively. Rates of complete response were 83% and 80% for 165 and 280 mg/m2 dose groups, respectively. The most common grade 3 or 4 adverse event was decreased neutrophil count."
      }
    ],
